        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 3:15AM EDT by NWS Jackson KY</headline>
        <description>Following recent rainfall, clearing skies and slackening winds
will lead to fog, especially in the valleys, and it will be dense
in some areas, with visibilities reduced below on half of a mile.

Those driving this morning, should exercise caution by slowing
down and by being prepared for sudden changes in visibility.
Allow plenty of room between your vehicle and the one in front of
you. Use low beam headlights and allow extra time to reach your
destination this morning.
</description>
